t:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":58160,"output_tokens":1515,"requests":3}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate .github/workflows/mirror-guard.yml as a consumer of the run-level signal and state whether/how the IO-vs-divergence distinction is surfaced there (distinct step name, annotation, or job summary) so AC1's 'distinguishable at the run level without reading the JSON body' holds for the CI surface, not just the module.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[".github/workflows/mirror-guard.yml line 52: `run: python -m rebar.mirror_guard --replication`","workflow comment (lines 6-10): the job 'FAILS (-> GitHub notification) only when ... divergence PERSISTS' — it exposes a single pass/fail, not IO-vs-divergence","AC1: 'An IO/reachability failure is DISTINGUISHABLE at the run level from a genuine SHA divergence, without reading the JSON body.'","mirror_guard.run already returns exit 2 for IO and 1 for divergence (src/rebar/mirror_guard.py lines 267-271), so the missing surfacing is in the workflow, not the module"],"finding":"The plan does not enumerate .github/workflows/mirror-guard.yml as a consumer of the run-level signal that AC1 targets. The workflow invokes `python -m rebar.mirror_guard --replication` and, per its own comments, FAILS (red run -> GitHub notification) on any non-zero exit; GitHub Actions renders exit 2 (IO/unreachable) and exit 1 (divergence) identically as a red X. Since AC1 requires the IO-vs-divergence distinction to be visible 'at the run level ... without reading the JSON body', this workflow is exactly the operator-facing surface where the distinction must be made visible, so it is an unenumerated consumer a fix would likely need to touch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0fe560f1e2f25a6b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC1 / Testing-Verification; consumer .github/workflows/mirror-guard.yml","norm_id":"n0f6a5eb87582f5b7","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A transient reachability dip yields exit 2; the workflow shows the same red X as a real divergence (exit 1), so an operator reading the Actions UI still cannot tell them apart 'at the run level'"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Locate the fix at the layer where AC1's 'run level' is actually read (the .github/workflows/mirror-guard.yml run, not just run()): specify how the already-existing exit-2/`check:io` signal is surfaced as a distinct, visible run-level outcome (e.g. a workflow step mapping exit 2 to a GitHub annotation or distinctly-labeled outcome), and add run-level (not only unit-level) verification, since run() already returns exit 2 today.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/mirror_guard.py:25 docstring: 'CLI exit codes: 0 all healthy · 1 unhealthy (divergence/drift) · 2 fetch/IO error.'","src/rebar/mirror_guard.py:267-269 already appends {\"check\": \"io\", ...} and returns _EXIT_ERROR (2)","tests/unit/test_mirror_guard.py:151-157 test_run_fetch_error_exit_2 already asserts code==2 and verdicts[-1]['check']=='io'; test_run_divergence_exit_1 already asserts code==1","Plan admits: 'The information ALREADY EXISTS in the output — the verdict carries \"check\": \"io\" distinctly'","AC1 requires distinguishability 'at the run level ... without reading the JSON body' but .github/workflows/mirror-guard.yml renders exit 1 and exit 2 identically as a red failed run; the plan never names the workflow as a change/verification site","ABSENCE: no plan step addresses how the exit-2/io signal is surfaced at the workflow/run UI (annotation, distinct step outcome, warning label)"],"finding":"The plan's chosen mechanism (unit tests on run()/verdict functions) does not reach the layer where AC1's 'run-level' conflation actually manifests; run() already returns exit code 2 for IO distinct from exit 1 for divergence, and both are already tested, so the plan risks re-proving existing behavior without surfacing the distinction at the GitHub Actions run level operators read.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3b532350c7a44fbb","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing / Verification section; AC1; AC4","norm_id":"nc1f343f92cbcfba4","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer adds/tightens unit tests, `pytest` and `make verify` pass, but the CI run for an unreachable host still shows the same undifferentiated red X the ticket complains about — AC1 unmet in practice"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a workflow step in mirror-guard.yml that inspects the CLI exit code and, on exit 2, emits a distinct run-level marker (e.g. `::warning::mirror-guard: host unreachable — could NOT verify mirror; not a divergence` or a distinctly-named failing step), while exit 1 keeps the plain divergence failure. Keep the existing unit tests but add coverage that the workflow/wrapper maps exit 2 to the unreachable-labeled outcome and exit 1 to the divergence outcome, satisfying AC1 at the layer the ticket describes.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test/proving step covering AC3: repeated (e.g. two consecutive) IO failures remain visible at the run level and are not silently swallowed as transient.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E6","E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC3: 'Repeated IO failures remain visible; a transient must not be silently swallowed, or this trades a false positive for a false negative.'","Testing section lists exactly two unit tests: unreachable fetch, and reachable-but-different SHAs — neither exercises repeated/successive IO failures or their persistent visibility."],"finding":"AC3 ('Repeated IO failures remain visible; a transient must not be silently swallowed') has no covering test or proving command; the Testing section only describes two tests — unreachable host and reachable-but-divergent SHAs — matching AC4/AC1/AC2 but not AC3.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8f411d4e0ef9f446","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC3 / Testing / Verification","norm_id":"n5566be454db0b47a","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two consecutive IO failures (as literally observed at 20:36Z and 20:49Z) should stay visible rather than being swallowed as transient — but nothing proves this behavior."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a third unit test in tests/unit/test_mirror_guard.py asserting that N successive unreachable-host runs each surface the distinct io/unreachable run-level state (no suppression), and reference it under Testing / Verification.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","c